00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.003
- I haven't had any regrets, you know,

00:00:42.003 --> 00:00:44.209
and it's sometimes really hard.

00:00:44.209 --> 00:00:46.972
I'll tell you a funny story.

00:00:46.972 --> 00:00:50.908
I remember right before
I got A Different World,

00:00:50.908 --> 00:00:53.010
I auditioned for Blossom.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:53.843
- Oh.

00:00:53.843 --> 00:00:54.676
- Do you remember the TV show Blossom?

00:00:54.676 --> 00:00:55.509
- Absolutely, yeah.

00:00:55.509 --> 00:00:57.573
- Do you remember her
friend, the young girl?

00:00:57.573 --> 00:00:58.525
- [Woman] Her six?

00:00:58.525 --> 00:00:59.651
- Her six.

00:00:59.651 --> 00:01:02.356
- I auditioned for Six, okay.

00:01:02.356 --> 00:01:04.225
And I had my hair up in a little pony tail

00:01:04.225 --> 00:01:05.131
with this little jumpsuit.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.663
I looked like I was about twelve.

00:01:06.663 --> 00:01:07.496
(laughter)

00:01:07.496 --> 00:01:09.601
Got the role, okay.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:12.132
Got the role to play Six.

00:01:12.132 --> 00:01:16.242
And I was like, I was
18, 19 years old then.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.574
I said, I looked at my
agent Nancy Rainford,

00:01:19.574 --> 00:01:21.396
I said Nancy, I can't do this.

00:01:21.396 --> 00:01:23.080
I just can't do it.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.982
I'm going to be miserable
playing a twelve year old

00:01:25.982 --> 00:01:26.888
on this show.

00:01:26.888 --> 00:01:28.513
I can't do this.

00:01:28.513 --> 00:01:29.346
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:01:29.346 --> 00:01:31.915
- And we had to turn it down.

00:01:31.915 --> 00:01:36.188
And let me tell you, them
folks were not happy.

00:01:36.188 --> 00:01:39.125
It's like who does this
girl think she is, you know,

00:01:39.125 --> 00:01:40.832
and that whole thing.

00:01:40.832 --> 00:01:44.558
But within two weeks, I
got A Different World.

00:01:44.558 --> 00:01:48.134
And that really taught me a lesson,

00:01:48.134 --> 00:01:51.551
which was, you know, to really listen to,

00:01:53.742 --> 00:01:57.074
and follow my gut, because
everything that shines

00:01:57.074 --> 00:01:59.849
isn't gold, you know what I mean?

00:01:59.849 --> 00:02:02.681
And so it really taught
me a very valuable lesson

00:02:02.681 --> 00:02:04.586
to just stay true to myself.

00:02:04.586 --> 00:02:06.861
If there's nothing that I haven't learned

00:02:06.861 --> 00:02:10.019
about this business,
it's really about staying

00:02:10.019 --> 00:02:11.769
true to why I'm here,

00:02:13.723 --> 00:02:17.833
why, you know, I started
acting in the first place

00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:20.340
and what's important to me.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.903
And keeping my artistic
integrity, as well as my creative,

00:02:24.903 --> 00:02:27.213
my personal integrity.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.675
And that was a big lesson for me.

00:02:29.675 --> 00:02:32.043
And let me tell you, that
was not an easy thing

00:02:32.043 --> 00:02:33.146
to turn down.

00:02:33.146 --> 00:02:35.782
You know, being a young actress,
you got this opportunity

00:02:35.782 --> 00:02:37.782
for this series regular.

00:02:39.427 --> 00:02:41.177
It's money, you know.

00:02:42.063 --> 00:02:44.025
But I just felt deep
down inside, I was like,

00:02:44.025 --> 00:02:46.695
something's coming your
way, just fall back.

00:02:46.695 --> 00:02:48.813
And then I got to meet,
you know, Debbie Allen.

00:02:48.813 --> 00:02:49.758
(applause)

00:02:49.758 --> 00:02:53.098
- I was always the class clown,
